Interchanging the names of the reciprocal variables yields the companion identity $\boxed{
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
\frac{dx}{2\pi}\,
e^{ix(p-p')}
=\delta(p-p')
}.$ The delta function is thus a continuous superposition of plane waves.

